Canonical directory view for text-to-SQL. Query ONLY this view (FROM orgs_llm).
Audience columns (works_with_*): a non-empty value is usually Directly or Indirectly.
Filter those with: col IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(col) != '' (do not require the word Yes).

View name: orgs_llm
Columns:
  - org_name (TEXT) [populated 86/86] examples: "PECT", "AXIS CLC", "Cotality"
  - department_or_unit (TEXT) [populated 18/86] examples: "Housing", "Home Energy", "Retrofit Team"
  - org_main_type (TEXT) [populated 86/86] examples: "Consultant or advisor", "Product manufacturer / supplier", "Academic department / group / network"
  - org_type_other_public (TEXT) [populated 3/86] examples: "General Further Education College", "Joint Industry/Government sector council", "A new organisation formed by a combination of local and combined authorities"
  - org_type_other_private (TEXT) [populated 9/86] examples: "Magazine", "Consumer Code", "Solution Provider"
  - org_type_other_nonprofit (TEXT) [populated 17/86] examples: "Charity", "Retrofit Hub", "Retrofit agency"
  - county (TEXT) [populated 86/86] examples: "Kent (England)", "Devon (England)", "Essex (England)"
  - postcode (TEXT) [populated 86/86] examples: "G2 3EX", "G4 9RH", "M1 6EU"
  - local_authority (TEXT) [populated 86/86] examples: "Arun", "Derby", "Leeds"
  - parish (TEXT) [populated 84/86] examples: "Frome", "Lewes", "Euxton"
